<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <!-- Question 7: Login Form with CSRF token -->
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Q7 - Login Form</title>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Login</h1>

    <form action="#" method="post">

        <label for="username">Username:</label>
        <input type="text" id="username" name="username" required>
        <br><br>

        <label for="password">Password:</label>
        <input type="password" id="password" name="password" required>
        <br><br>

        <!-- A CSRF (Cross-Site Request Forgery) token is a unique, secret value generated
             by the server and embedded in the form. When the form is submitted, the server
             checks that this token matches the one it issued. This proves the request really
             came from the site's own form and not from a malicious site tricking the user's
             browser into submitting a forged request, since an attacker would not know the
             correct token value. -->
        <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="a1b2c3d4e5f6dummy">

        <input type="submit" value="Login">

    </form>

</body>
</html>
